### Load test artifacts ###
# Tooling and the protocol doc are committed; the outputs are not.
# A single run produces 40-100MB of .jtl, and the seed dump is over 1GB -
# past GitHub's 100MB file limit, in a public repo.
# JMeter raw results, anywhere. The listener writes popping_results.jtl into
# whatever directory JMeter was launched from, so this is not confined to
# docs/load-test - a 1.5GB one was sitting in the repo root.
*.jtl
docs/load-test/dump.sql
# Generated JMeter HTML reports: ~3.9MB each, mostly vendored JS/CSS.
# The evidence worth keeping is small and textual (metrics CSV, steady verdict,
# run metadata) - commit those explicitly instead.
docs/load-test/*report*/
jmeter.log
